ield/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451277}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e41c04ee-99fe-56c1-8773-ea0949cc66d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42377" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $L,M,$ and $N?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $ML$ is well defined\n- **II.** The product $MN$ is well defined\n- **III.** The product $LN$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $L$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $M$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $N$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $M$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $M$ and $L$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{L}_{2\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $M$ and $3$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $M$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $L$ and $3$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $L$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $L$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{L}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, while statement I is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b747550b-0a4a-5f3d-86b4-30ddaca87768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450648} {:answer/id #uuid "f90dfbaa-1eb7-5028-8821-63442d778562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f90dfbaa-1eb7-5028-8821-63442d778562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649} :answer-field/id #uuid "623efc55-bdf4-53da-9936-ec2df1772b9d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451278} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7ca6a7b-d2c1-579c-8b4e-c3fc51e76679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450650} {:answer/id #uuid "460bc98c-aa4d-5008-abd2-b4b13e84f625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7ca6a7b-d2c1-579c-8b4e-c3fc51e76679" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450650} :answer-field/id #uuid "5059dfed-f97b-5c68-860f-943b60870dcb" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451279} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fd12d0-0b82-5d63-b678-fdb08097e4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450652} {:answer/id #uuid "dd3ba80b-43c0-5469-926f-886110b94004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20fd12d0-0b82-5d63-b678-fdb08097e4e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450652} :answer-field/id #uuid "d414d56d-e135-5893-a7d7-26e4a83fd3f2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "628bddc5-7db2-5c2d-bca2-c9a2f11c4f87" :question/math-academy-id "q-42381" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The product $OP$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $OR$ is well defined\n\n- **III.** The product $PR$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $P$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $R$ is a $1\\times 3$ row vector.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $O$ and $2$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $O$ and $1$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $1$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statements II and III are false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f38167e2-3c1d-5c00-9691-ba8e6ac6fdce" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Dimension of the Product of Two Matrices Given the Dimensions of the Factors" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783 :topic/title "Conformability for Matrix Multiplication"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447a88e0-6091-5ac0-9834-0b06c2b6da42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\times 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336671} {:answer/id #uuid "5761b146-8cbf-5d87-97ae-a54747bdf58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\times 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336835} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0d3dd2-c61b-5322-93f0-d47718dacdc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\times 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337156} {:answer/id #uuid "906ba5cf-0c86-5c6a-a079-c82f2917e945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\times 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337341} {:answer/id #uuid "ca878198-1b18-5ab0-904e-b20db81eaa43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id 